<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1d03f3c8c21a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5978] The Republic of Korea’s Personal Information Protection Committee (PIPC) has launched an investigation to follow up on allegations about the collection and processing of personal biometric data by Sam Altman’s digital ID and crypto side project potentially falling afoul of local laws." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5978" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/230b2378157b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5978] The PIPC says its investigations will cover “the overall collection and processing of sensitive information and overseas transfer of personal information under the Personal Information Protection Act.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5978" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2724e832eaa1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5979] \"Worldcoin was designed to protect individual privacy and has built a robust privacy program. The project complies with all laws and regulations governing the processing of personal data in the markets where Worldcoin is available, including but not limited to Argentina's Personal Data Protection Act 25.326 (Ley de Protección de los Datos Personales),\" the Worldcoin Foundation said in an email sent to International Business Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5979" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2eea0111fdae> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Worldcoin Regulatory Scrutiny Grows: Argentina Launches Investigation Over Data Privacy" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5979" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/35206dbb13e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[7564] Since its launch in July 2023, Worldcoin has faced regulatory investigations in countries such as Germany, France, the United Kingdom, and Kenya, with Argentina initiating an investigation in August. [5978] The Republic of Korea’s Personal Information Protection Committee (PIPC) has launched an investigation to follow up on allegations about the collection and processing of personal biometric data by Sam Altman’s digital ID and crypto side project potentially falling afoul of local laws." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4ca3426ad5ea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Another government is raising an eyebrow at Worldcoin’s iris biometrics bonanza." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5978" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5517cb2c26e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Argentina says it's investigating Worldcoin over data privacy" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/56bf199630d6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5979] \"Worldcoin was designed to protect individual privacy and has built a robust privacy program. The project complies with all laws and regulations governing the processing of personal data in the markets where Worldcoin is available, including but not limited to Argentina's Personal Data Protection Act 25.326 (Ley de Protección de los Datos Personales),\" the Worldcoin Foundation said in an email sent to International Business Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5979" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6dd18d9b92f3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"The case reached public notoriety in recent weeks due to the procedure of scanning the face and iris of numerous people in exchange for economic compensation in different parts of the Autonomous City of Buenos Aires and the provinces of Buenos Aires, Córdoba, Mendoza and Black river,\" the agency added." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5979" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/71f6d6ffeb6a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the collection of facial and iris information from individuals at ten locations across South Korea." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/75fa645ad0ab> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[7565] Argentina is launching an investigation into the Worldcoin Foundation, the identity-focused crypto project co-created by Sam Altman. [7567] Cofounded by Open AI CEO Sam Altman, Worldcoin is a cryptocurrency project that aims to create a global system for digital identification." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7ce61ff3789f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "South Korea privacy regulator to investigate Worldcoin’s biometrics handling" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5978" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/88ea6fb78807> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[7567] Worldcoin, known for its iris-biometric cryptocurrency project, has recently been spotlighted in Argentina. [7564] Worldcoin, known for its ambitious goal of creating a global digital identity through iris scanning technology, has come under scrutiny in several countries for the legality of its operations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7567" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/943b547005b9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Argentina Investigates Worldcoin Amid Mounting Regulatory Pressure" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7567" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/96a4c829d6ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On paper, the really interesting part of Worldcoin's concept is that the iris scan is discarded after reading, avoiding the storage of that highly sensitive data." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5979" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a5f7f3a3061d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Unlike traditional cryptocurrencies, Worldcoin offers users free tokens, but there’s a catch: participants must undergo an eye scan upon registration." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7567" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/af5ea445d4b8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[7564] Since its launch in July 2023, Worldcoin has faced regulatory investigations in countries such as Germany, France, the United Kingdom, and Kenya, with Argentina initiating an investigation in August. [5978] The Republic of Korea’s Personal Information Protection Committee (PIPC) has launched an investigation to follow up on allegations about the collection and processing of personal biometric data by Sam Altman’s digital ID and crypto side project potentially falling afoul of local laws." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ccbef5884c28> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5979] \"Worldcoin was designed to protect individual privacy and has built a robust privacy program. The project complies with all laws and regulations governing the processing of personal data in the markets where Worldcoin is available, including but not limited to Argentina's Personal Data Protection Act 25.326 (Ley de Protección de los Datos Personales),\" the Worldcoin Foundation said in an email sent to International Business Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5979" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dad7bd26f7aa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Worldcoin, known for its ambitious goal of creating a global digital identity through iris scanning technology, has come under scrutiny in several countries for the legality of its operations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd5808d2b7e1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This biometric verification ensures that each participant is a genuine human, preventing bots or AI algorithms from exploiting the system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7567" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e09dbeb816dd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[7564] the collection of facial and iris information from individuals at ten locations across South Korea." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7564" .

