<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1acc07a7ce64> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In January, Hong Kong’s privacy commissioner staged raids on Worldcoin’s offices, citing similar concerns about data privacy laws." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5978" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2df872d36170> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The PIPC says its investigations will cover “the overall collection and processing of sensitive information and overseas transfer of personal information under the Personal Information Protection Act.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5978" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/371a075cc201> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Public Information Access Agency will \"thoroughly analyze\" the processes and practices used in relation to the collection, storage and use of personal data, the government said in a statement." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/54d567bc0689> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Argentina said earlier this week that a government information agency is launching an investigation into the Worldcoin Foundation, the identity-focused crypto project co-created by Sam Altman." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8a3803b1ccfa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The raid came on the heels of the announcement from Kenya's Ministry of the Interior that it has suspended Worldcoin's operations over concerns about the company's ongoing \"registration of citizens through the collection of eyeball/iris data.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5979" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a0ecd1bb2868> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Argentine Agency for Access to Public Information (AAIP) commenced its investigation into Worldcoin over the legality of its data collection." ;
